# __NAME__

`.about/` holds this project's decisions: read `.about/adr/` before proposing a change to how it is
built, and don't reopen what an ADR already settled (ADR stack).

The code is on GitHub, `__OWNER__/__NAME__`: pull requests go there, through `gh` (ADR stack).

## Tools and checks

mise pins every tool and runs every task: `mise run check` is what CI runs, so run it before a
commit is pushed (ADR stack).

## Commits and Git hooks

Commit messages follow `.hathi.yml`, which the Git hooks check: @.hathi.yml (ADR stack)

The Git hooks are in `.githooks/` and run `hathi`, which `mise.toml` pins. Turn them on once per
clone with `mise run setup`, which installs the tools and runs `git config core.hooksPath
.githooks` (ADR stack).
